#question(title: [Challenge])[
  Compute #h(1em)
  $display(A = sum_(n = 1)^oo n/(3^n))$
  #h(1em) and #h(1em)
  $display(B = sum_(n = 1)^oo (n^2)/(3^n))$

  #box(width: 1fr, line(length: 100%, stroke: .5pt))

  + What is the value of the sum
    $display(sum_(n = 0)^oo x^n)$ ?
  + Use derivatives to relate
    $display(sum_n^oo x^n)$ and
    $display(sum_n^oo n x^(n - 1))$.
  + Compute
    $display(sum_(n = 1)^oo n x^(n - 1))$.
    #h(1em) Then compute
    $display(sum_(n = 1)^oo n x^n)$.
  + Compute the value of series $A$.
  + Compute the value of series $B$.
]
